-- EXPECT-ERROR: `log` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`
mod Main do
  -- R1 stage C reject witness (2026-08-10) — the same decisive property as
  -- t166, moved from the PROGRAM to a single FUNCTION. `main` here takes no
  -- capability parameter at all, so stages A/B have nothing to say: this
  -- program is ambient, and every earlier check passes. Every `needs` line
  -- is truthful, Check 1b passes, the ceiling passes, R3 has nothing to
  -- forge.
  --
  -- It is still rejected, because `log` was HANDED `Cap(IO.Console)` and its
  -- transitive reach leaves that ceiling. This is the guarantee stage C adds
  -- over stage B: it composes per function and per dependency, so a library
  -- function's bound holds without the whole program opting in.
  --
  -- As in t166 the violation lives one frame down, in the helper: a grant an
  -- attacker could evade by moving the call away would bound nothing. Accept
  -- companion t174 is this file minus the `save` call inside `log`.
  needs IO.Console
  needs IO.FileWrite

  fn save(msg : String) : () do
    match file_write("/tmp/t174_out", msg) do
      Ok(_)  -> ()
      Err(_) -> ()
    end
  end

  fn log(_cap : Cap(IO.Console), msg : String) : () do
    save(msg)
    println(msg)
  end

  fn main() : () do
    ()
  end
end
